%% DM26-0670

%% From an agent's declared topics to the broker's decision, as built (2026-11-04, policy-enforcement.md, "Decisions", authority-model.md). Applying the catalog is the
%% administrator's sign-off: there is no separate grants document. The issuance steps in full are general/workload_certificate_issuance.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Code as the agent's code<br/>(PolarAgent::TOPICS)
    participant Res as resolve.nu / render.nu
    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant K as Kubernetes API
    participant CI as cert-issuer<br/>(floor)
    participant CA as credentials agent<br/>(authority model)
    participant Init as the workload's pod<br/>(polar-init, custodian)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker

    Res->>Code: IMAGE --scaffold, with POLAR_SERVED_WORKLOADS (a pod in a scratch namespace, cached by digest)
    Code-->>Res: the full set: declared topics with their access, implied topics each with its rule
    Res->>Res: the target's sets, the scheduler's family already exact (one per served agent),<br/>and a warning for each declared topic with no other side in the target
    Note over Res: catalog-wide, infra/tests/catalog-topics.nu fails on a one-sided topic<br/>that gives no reason, from every agent built from the workspace
    Res->>Res: each workload's declared topics into CREDENTIALS_AGENT_AUTHORITY_MODEL,<br/>the bootstrap services' into CERT_ISSUER_BOOTSTRAP
    Admin->>K: apply the catalog (up.nu, or the signed publish Flux applies): the sign-off
    K->>CA: the model, a variable read once at its start, so its pod rolls for a change
    K->>CI: cert-issuer's floor

    Note over Init,CA: a workload's pod starts, or rejuvenates
    Init->>CA: the sealed token buys the custodian's certificate, through the observer
    Init->>CA: the custodian asks for the workload's certificates, over Cassini
    CA->>CA: identity from the token, then this workload's declared topics and groups from the model
    CA-->>Init: certificate: DNS identity, p:pub:topic and p:sub:topic for each declared topic,<br/>g:group for each group, i:uid and i:pod for one of many instances<br/>(implied topics are not written: they follow from the identity and the groups)
    Note over CI: the bootstrap services are signed by cert-issuer, with the topics and groups of their own floor entry

    Init->>Bk: (the agent) connect with that certificate. The floor is read once, after the handshake
    Bk->>Bk: on each subscribe and publish,<br/>with a cache per connection:<br/>Cedar first (permit and forbid<br/>both override), else the floor:<br/>implied from the identity and its g: groups,<br/>declared from the p: names, else refuse
    Note over Admin,Bk: a change to an agent's topics is a change to the catalog, applied like any other: the credentials agent restarts with the new model,<br/>and the agent has it with its next certificate and connection, within the hour. Cedar can act at once meanwhile
